          <h2>Questions members ask</h2>
          <h3>Which Blue Cross plan do I have?</h3>
          <p>Look at your benefit card or your welcome documents. The name on the card, such as Medavie Blue Cross, Pacific Blue Cross or Alberta Blue Cross, tells you which organization administers your plan, which app to download and where to send questions. Plans share the Blue Cross name and symbol while running their own member services.</p>
          <h3>Does Blue Cross cover acupuncture?</h3>
          <p>Many Blue Cross group plans include acupuncture as a paramedical category, with an annual maximum. The treatment needs to come from a registered acupuncturist, and the receipt needs to show that registration. Confirm the category in your member app. Some plans leave it out.</p>
          <h3>Can my clinic bill Blue Cross directly?</h3>
          <p>Often, yes. Clinics registered with your Blue Cross organization can submit the claim at your appointment, and you pay only the part your plan leaves with you. Ask when you book, and bring your card so the clinic has your policy and member numbers.</p>
          <h3>Does Blue Cross cover physiotherapy without a referral?</h3>
          <p>Physiotherapy is a direct access service in much of Canada, meaning you can book a physiotherapist without seeing a doctor first. Coverage is a separate question from booking, and a small number of plans ask for a physician note for some services. Your plan summary states any referral rule that applies to you.</p>

          <h2>Find care that fits your Blue Cross plan</h2>
          <p>Confirm your region first, then match the treatment to its category. Browse the <a href="/#directory">WellFinder directory</a> to compare clinics across Canada, and open pages such as <a href="/clinics-pelvic-floor-physiotherapy">pelvic floor physiotherapy clinics</a> and <a href="/clinics-tmj-massage">TMJ massage clinics</a> to see providers and how their visits bill. Before you book, check the balance for the category in your member app and ask the clinic whether it can bill your Blue Cross organization directly.</p>
          <p>WellFinder is an independent directory and is not affiliated with any Blue Cross organization. This guide explains common features of Blue Cross plans in Canada. Your employer plan governs your coverage, and your Blue Cross organization or plan administrator can confirm what your plan pays.</p>

